Summary:
During today’s development session, we continued working on the backend of the GitHub profile evaluator project. We focused on enhancing the evaluation functionality by incorporating a separate utility for score calculation. The required scoring function was imported into the controller file and connected with the existing API logic. We ensured that the GitHub user and repository data fetched using Axios were properly passed to this function. The overall flow of the application was tested to confirm that the integration worked smoothly without affecting existing features.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, we successfully integrated the scoring mechanism into the profile evaluation process. The application is now capable of generating a score based on the fetched GitHub data, making the output more meaningful. This approach improved code organization by separating business logic into a utility file. It also made the codebase more modular and easier to maintain or extend in the future. As a result, the project now follows better development practices and is more aligned with real-world application design.
